  "id": "DrugBank_DB06014 - MONDO_10679",
  "verbalization": "Eteplirsen is implicated in the pathogenesis of Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy (DMD) through a multi-step pathway involving the indication of Muscular Dystrophy and Becker Muscular Dystrophy. The evidence suggests that Eteplirsen may act as a therapeutic agent for DMD, as it is linked to both Becker Muscular Dystrophy and Muscular Dystrophy, which are both subtypes of muscular dystrophy with overlapping pathophysiology. The presence of Deflazacort, a known inhibitor of the dystrophin-glycoprotein complex, in the indication chain further supports a potential role in the pathogenesis of DMD. The shared indication of Deflazacort with Eteplirsen implies a possible mechanism of action that could target the same biological pathways, such as dystrophin synthesis or degradation. The integration of these pathways suggests that Eteplirsen may exert its therapeutic effect by modulating the dystrophin-related pathways, potentially offering a novel treatment approach for DMD. The evidence is supported by the presence of a direct indication chain from Eteplirsen to Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
